WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.435
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show,"

00:00:03.435 --> 00:00:05.304
ladies and gentlemen!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.304 --> 00:00:07.740
Thank you for being here.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.442
Well, guys,
here's some good news.

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:12.145
Last night, an FDA panel
gave the green light

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:15.148
to the Pfizer vaccine for
kids between the ages of

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:16.449
5 and 11.

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:20.587
That's right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:22.855
That's right -- kids' vaccines
are the best way to prevent

00:00:22.855 --> 00:00:24.624
the two things parents
fear the most --

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:26.593
COVID and homeschooling.

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:29.929
"I don't know. 3 goes into 5.
I don't know!

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:31.597
I'm not a math teacher!"

00:00:31.597 --> 00:00:32.865
Yep, this is great.

00:00:32.865 --> 00:00:34.800
In a few weeks, you're gonna
see bouncers outside

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.870
Chuck E. Cheese
checking vaccine cards.

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:40.140
"Not today, Timmy. Sorry."

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:44.077
Kids could get the shot
as soon as next week.

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:47.913
Great timing -- right after they
go door-to-door on Halloween.

00:00:47.913 --> 00:00:49.315
"You want to
move it up three days?

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:52.318
Who's talking to who here?"

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:53.719
Here's how
the vaccine will work.

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:56.455
Older kids can get Pfizer,
younger kids can get Moderna,

00:00:56.455 --> 00:00:59.892
and the middle child
can get Johnson &amp; Johnson.

00:00:59.892 --> 00:01:03.930
Come on. They'll figure it out.
They'll figure it out.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.965
Pretty soon, you're gonna see a
vaccine center parking lot

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:09.669
with white tents, orange cones,
waving in little toy Jeeps.

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:12.005
[ Imitates revving ]

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:16.509
Some parents said that
they aren't sure if

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:19.311
they're comfortable giving
their kids the vaccine.

00:01:19.311 --> 00:01:20.513
Then they went back to
feeding them

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:21.681
Dunkaroos for breakfast.

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:25.451
They're like,
"Yeah, this -- There you go.

00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:27.586
You're someone else's problem
for the next six hours.

00:01:27.586 --> 00:01:29.421
Go enjoy."

00:01:29.421 --> 00:01:30.556
Some news from Washington.

00:01:30.556 --> 00:01:32.324
This morning, Senate Democrats
rolled out

00:01:32.324 --> 00:01:34.159
a new tax proposal
that would only target

00:01:34.159 --> 00:01:37.129
the 700 richest Americans

00:01:37.129 --> 00:01:39.265
as a way to help
Biden's spending plan.

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:42.134
So that includes
Elon Musk, Jeff Bezos,

00:01:42.134 --> 00:01:44.771
and Flo, the
Progressive Insurance lady.

00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:47.240
It's tough for billionaires.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.708
If you'd like to sponsor one,

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:52.645
you can make a difference
for just $34 million a day.

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:56.715
Just text "Billions" to 01528.

00:01:56.715 --> 00:01:58.684
You know cash is tight for
billionaires when

00:01:58.684 --> 00:02:02.621
their flights in space have
a layover in Cleveland.

00:02:02.621 --> 00:02:03.723
But by this afternoon,

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:05.724
Democrats scrapped
the tax on billionaires,

00:02:05.724 --> 00:02:08.828
and now they might
tax millionaires instead.

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:11.297
Yep. When they heard that,
Kim and Kylie were like, "Yes!"

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:14.067
while Khloé, Kourtney,
and Kendall were like, "No!"

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:19.606
Well, Iowa Senator
Chuck Grassley, who is 88,

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:24.043
recently announced that he is
running for re-election in 2022.

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:25.845
And while a lot of critics say
that he's too old

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:28.381
and should retire,
I think he's still got it.

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.583
Just watch this clip from today.

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:33.953
-I...

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:38.224
don't...

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:41.293
When you don't hold
your own accountable --

00:02:41.293 --> 00:02:46.532
Let's not forget about
Obama-Biden administration.

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:48.568
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:53.473
-It's not a good sign when
your staff is nearby

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:54.706
with a set of jumper cables.

00:02:54.706 --> 00:02:56.242
You know, they're like...

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:59.913
"Right goes on right nipple?"

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:03.816
When an aide said,
"Senator, are you alright?",

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:06.352
he was like,
"There's a senator here?"

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:09.855
"No...

00:03:09.855 --> 00:03:11.691
but..."

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:17.063
What? What are we doing?

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:19.399
I think the whole world just
needs to take the weekend.

00:03:19.399 --> 00:03:20.666
-Yeah.
-Tomorrow's the weekend.

00:03:20.666 --> 00:03:22.001
Just take the weekend.
We'll come back Monday.

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:23.903
We'll figure it all out. Yeah.

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:24.971
Some movie news.

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:26.839
Today, Pixar released
the first trailer

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:29.708
for their Buzz Lightyear
origin story.

00:03:29.708 --> 00:03:32.111
-Ooh!
-Yeah, a Buzz Lightyear prequel.

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:33.779
It's about how he
first goes to space

00:03:33.779 --> 00:03:36.416
as a publicity stunt for
Jeff Bezos.

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:39.485
But the prequel
looks interesting.

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:41.821
For instance, I had no idea that
when Buzz's family arrived

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:45.391
at Ellis Island, they changed
their name from Lightyearinelli.

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:46.859
-Really?

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:53.766
-"Buzzscucci Lightyearinelli,"
yeah.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.467
Did you guys see this?

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:57.169
There's a new dating show
in the U.K.,

00:03:57.169 --> 00:03:58.937
and it's kind of similar to
"The Bachelor,"

00:03:58.937 --> 00:04:00.305
but there's one big difference.

00:04:00.305 --> 00:04:01.440
Just take a look at this.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:08.581
-David, who do you think is
a love trap?

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:12.685
♪♪

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:14.353
-Cherie.

00:04:14.353 --> 00:04:17.223
-Whoa!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:20.893
Whoa!

00:04:22.461 --> 00:04:25.365
-Wow!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:31.770
-Gosh!

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:33.940
-It got awkward when he was
like, "Wait, I meant Becca.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.675
I'm sorry."

00:04:35.675 --> 00:04:37.009
Yeah, it's just like
"The Bachelor,"

00:04:37.009 --> 00:04:38.611
but instead of being
escorted out in a limo,

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:41.747
they were taken away in
an ambulance.

00:04:41.747 --> 00:04:42.915
Some more entertainment news.

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:44.850
I read that Netflix
is looking to build a new

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:48.220
TV and film production studio
in New Jersey.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.556
Yeah. And, apparently,
Netflix is even coming out with

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:51.890
some New Jersey-themed TV shows.

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:52.925
-Really?

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:54.026
-Yeah.
I'll show you what I mean.

00:04:54.026 --> 00:04:55.861
First up, there's
"Bridge and Tunnelton."

00:04:55.861 --> 00:04:57.696
-Oh!

00:04:57.696 --> 00:05:01.267
-Next, there's "Squid Game:
Just the Tracksuits."

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:06.639
Next up, instead of the show
"You," there's "Youz."

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:09.041
-Hey!

00:05:09.675 --> 00:05:13.546
-And, finally,
there's "Ohhhhh-zark."

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:17.116
Come on. You liked that.

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:20.519
"Ohhhhh-zark."

00:05:20.519 --> 00:05:21.787
Well, some business news.

00:05:21.787 --> 00:05:23.488
The outdoor-clothing
company Patagonia

00:05:23.488 --> 00:05:26.892
just introduced its own
collection of natural wine.

00:05:26.892 --> 00:05:28.827
Finally answering the question,

00:05:28.827 --> 00:05:31.497
"What is the whitest sentence
you've ever heard?"

00:05:32.965 --> 00:05:36.636
Wow! Patagonia wine.
-Patagonia wine.

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:38.070
-Natural.
-Natural wine.

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:39.204
Sorry. I apologize.

00:05:39.204 --> 00:05:40.373
Listen to this.

00:05:40.373 --> 00:05:42.608
The largest 3D-printed
neighborhood in the U.S.

00:05:42.608 --> 00:05:45.445
is currently being built
in Austin, Texas.

00:05:45.445 --> 00:05:47.046
The next time a
Texas sheriff says,

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:48.914
"This town ain't big enough
for the two of us,"

00:05:48.914 --> 00:05:51.484
the outlaw can say, "Hold on,
I'll print more."

00:05:52.217 --> 00:05:53.319
This is interesting.

00:05:53.319 --> 00:05:54.687
New research found
that Americans get

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:59.325
30 minutes less exercise than
they did 200 years ago.

00:06:02.761 --> 00:06:05.231
Well, people in the 1800s
also gargled with gasoline,

00:06:05.231 --> 00:06:08.167
so let's maybe call it a wash,
right, don't you think?

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:11.904
Yeah, people in the 1800s led
healthier, more energetic lives

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:14.673
and made it to
the ripe old age of 28.

00:06:15.741 --> 00:06:17.576
And, finally,
I saw that a guy in Hawaii

00:06:17.576 --> 00:06:19.478
who got into
some trouble with the law

00:06:19.478 --> 00:06:22.048
tried to flee the scene
in a pretty unique way.

00:06:22.048 --> 00:06:23.282
Watch this.

00:06:23.282 --> 00:06:26.185
-On Hawaii Island,
police say this man fled on

00:06:26.185 --> 00:06:30.556
a stolen lawnmower after
starting a small brush fire.

00:06:30.556 --> 00:06:32.324
Witnesses took video of the man

00:06:32.324 --> 00:06:36.128
riding the stolen push lawnmower
down Highway 11.

00:06:36.128 --> 00:06:39.832
-I think it would have been
faster if he actually

00:06:39.832 --> 00:06:42.768
just pushed the lawnmower
and just ran with it.

00:06:42.768 --> 00:06:45.037
But he had the last laugh
when he held a Weedwacker

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:47.006
in the air and took off
like a helicopter.

00:06:47.006 --> 00:06:48.741
"So long, suckas!"

00:06:49.342 --> 00:06:52.511
Did you guys hear about
the Volvo recall?

00:06:52.511 --> 00:06:54.379
It's not good.
Here, take a look at this.

00:06:54.379 --> 00:06:56.349
-Volvo is recalling
another 195,000 vehicles

00:06:56.349 --> 00:06:57.517
in the U.S.

00:06:57.517 --> 00:07:00.219
because the driver-side airbag
can explode.

00:07:00.219 --> 00:07:03.922
-Explode?!

00:07:03.922 --> 00:07:06.358
Oh, man, I just bought a Volvo.

00:07:06.358 --> 00:07:08.361
-I'm sorry about that, Tariq.

00:07:08.361 --> 00:07:11.330
-It's okay.
I still have my old Ram Truck.

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:14.833
I've had it turned off for a
while, but it should be fine.

00:07:14.833 --> 00:07:16.835
-Oh.

00:07:16.835 --> 00:07:18.937
-What "Oh?" "Oh" what?

00:07:18.937 --> 00:07:21.440
-Roll the clip.

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:23.575
-Ram is recalling more than
130,000 trucks

00:07:23.575 --> 00:07:26.245
because they could catch fire
even when turned off.

00:07:26.245 --> 00:07:29.648
-What?!

00:07:29.648 --> 00:07:31.116
How am I supposed
to take my kids

00:07:31.116 --> 00:07:32.885
trick-or-treating this weekend?

00:07:32.885 --> 00:07:34.887
-I don't know. I'm sorry, Tariq.

00:07:34.887 --> 00:07:38.791
-I guess I could give them some
snacks from around the house.

00:07:38.791 --> 00:07:40.693
I mean, I just bought
these really good

00:07:40.693 --> 00:07:44.997
Citterio-branded Premium
Italian-style Salame Sticks.

00:07:44.997 --> 00:07:46.599
-The CDC is issuing
a recall on the

00:07:46.599 --> 00:07:50.769
Citterio-branded Premium
Italian-style Salame Sticks.

00:07:50.769 --> 00:07:53.038
-Oh, come on!

00:07:53.038 --> 00:07:56.108
-I'm sure -- I'm sure
you'll figure something out.

00:07:56.108 --> 00:07:57.276
-What else do I have?

00:07:57.276 --> 00:07:58.877
Like, what else do I even
have in my kitchen?

00:07:58.877 --> 00:08:02.014
I guess there's some
red, yellow, and white onions,

00:08:02.014 --> 00:08:04.249
but I don't even know where
they were grown.

00:08:04.249 --> 00:08:06.352
-The FDA says that
people should throw away any

00:08:06.352 --> 00:08:08.654
red, yellow, or white onions

00:08:08.654 --> 00:08:10.690
if you don't know where
they were grown.

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:13.225
-Fine!

00:08:13.225 --> 00:08:15.995
I'll just give them
the Butterball ground-turkey

00:08:15.995 --> 00:08:18.397
products I have saved
for Thanksgiving.

00:08:18.397 --> 00:08:19.899
-More than 14,000 pounds of

00:08:19.899 --> 00:08:22.534
Butterball's ground-turkey
products are being recalled.

00:08:22.534 --> 00:08:26.138
-Man, I'm getting so mad,
I'm gonna need to take

00:08:26.138 --> 00:08:28.407
blood-pressure medication!

00:08:28.407 --> 00:08:29.708
-Recall alert this morning.

00:08:29.708 --> 00:08:32.544
It's for anyone who takes
a blood-pressure medication.

00:08:32.544 --> 00:08:34.346
-That's it. I'm done.

00:08:34.346 --> 00:08:35.914
-Alright, Tariq Trotter,
everybody.

00:08:35.914 --> 00:08:36.982
Tariq --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:36.982 --> 00:08:38.217
Tariq Trotter.
We'll figure it out.

00:08:38.217 --> 00:08:39.218
Tariq's gonna cool down.

